let's bring in republican congressman  tony gonzalez he represents the largest  border district in texas stretching over  800 miles of the border  congressman good to be with you there's  a lot of criticism of the vice president  for going to el paso instead of going to  the mcallen hidalgo area in the heart of  the rio grande valley sector the vice  president's office said  that of el paso it represents larger  border dynamics and it is a critical  critical part of understanding the human  experience of migration but take a look  at these numbers  the rio grande valley the year today two  hundred and nineteen  thousand seven hundred and eighty eight  border encounters versus el paso  eighty five thousand two hundred and  seventy three what's the difference  between what the vice president would  see in the rio grande valley sector as  opposed to what she's seeing today in el  paso  yeah the the border is very different  throughout you know i represent over 40  percent of the border and it's just very  diverse  you know kamala's first visit to the  border as vice president  has been a huge flop you know she's just  kind of parachuted in  uh only listen to folks for only a few  hours that's not how you  listen to folks and that's not how you  respond to it what's happening in el  paso is much different than what's  happening in the del rio sector  or in the big bend sector or laredo or  rio grande valley  i'll give you an example they're saying  they're making progress well in  culberson county just very close to el  paso  there was there was a 35 year old man  traveling with his 15 year old son  from ecuador they make the trek well  guess what his 15 year old son  dies because they got separated from a  group he died a horrible death uh  you know not having any water that's  that's the reality  of what's happening on the ground  migrants are dying yeah yeah i mean  there's no question about that and as  the heat continues to build  as well uh it gets more and more  dangerous and even chad wolfe was saying  that he doesn't expect there to be the  typical  decline in migration during the hot  summer months but  i just wanted to point out because we we  do like to be fair and balanced here  at fox news she is getting she kamil  harris is getting a lot of criticism for  going to el paso  but back in march a congressional  delegation led by the house minority  leader kevin mccarthy  went to el paso here's what he said  during that visit  i came down here because i heard of the  crisis it's more than a crisis  this is a human heartbreak the sad part  about all this  it didn't have to happen this crisis  is created by the presidential policies  of this new administration  so he was very critical of the  administration but nobody criticized him  for going to el paso saying oh you  missed the big story in the rio grande  valley sector so why is the vice  president coming in for so much  criticism for doing the same thing  you know i was on that visit with kevin  mccarthy back in march  and what we saw in el paso then were  record numbers  that processing center where she visited  today  it was beyond at capacity now i've also  visited that same processing center  since then and the numbers have gone  down in the el paso county  in the el paso uh sector but there's  other sectors that have  the numbers have only increased del rio  and rio grande valley in particular  so what i get at is this border crisis  is always shifting  and always moving you can't just land  somewhere  talk to somebody for a few hours and  then become an expert  you really have to dedicate the time and  effort from all of it from el paso to  del rio to eagle  uh to the the rio grande valley little  radio sector  all of it is important i hope this is  the first of many visits  that she makes to really tackle this  problem you know something really  popped out at me when the vice  president's delegation landed  there in el paso congresswoman veronica  escobar  said to the press pool that was  assembled there welcome to the new  ellis island making comparisons between  el paso  and the millions of people who came  through ellis island  in a wave of immigration to the united  states in the early 20th century  what did you make of that comment  there's a big difference  look we're a nation of immigrants we are  also a nation of laws  and our laws must be followed  what i make out of it is we need to  reform  our legal immigration process at the  same time  we have to uphold our laws people don't  feel  safe encouraging folks to make this trek  illegally  is wrong we need to reform our legal  immigration system  welcome those who want to come live the  american dream but do it through a legal  fashion  when we start encouraging folks to come  over illegally  which is exactly what this  administration has done  that is the wrong approach that that uh  unravels  america we stand for law and order  congressman tony gonzalez good to have  you with us today to kick off our  coverage and again we're expecting to  hear from the vice president coming up  in the next half hour so appreciate your  time hope you have a good weekend thank  you  thank you sir
 

